<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>The half-turn operator on affine functions</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This subsection establishes a conditional half-turn estimate for affine
observables. After rescaling <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X-y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X-y</annotation></semantics></math> by the Gaussian scale
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we show that the half-turn nearly maps every affine
function with mean zero to its negative. The proof combines a Duhamel
representation of the half-turn with covariance identities for the
rescaled conditional law.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proof of : From affine estimates to the half-turn bound ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, this estimate will be applied to
the conditional affine part of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}w</annotation></semantics></math> in the proof of
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first fix <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and work under the conditional law of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>
given <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=y</annotation></semantics></math>. The bounds below are uniform in <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and will later be
integrated over <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. To put the Gaussian confinement and harmonic
dynamics on unit scale, set</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\coloneqq\frac{X-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptq_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\coloneqq\frac{X-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptq_{y}\coloneqq\Law(W\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The density of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and the scaled potential gradient are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{y}(\mathrm{d}w)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)-\frac{1}{2}\|w\|^{2}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}w\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{y}(w)\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}(\mathrm{d}w)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)-\frac{1}{2}\|w\|^{2}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}w\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{y}(w)\coloneqq\sqrt{\eta}\,\nabla V(y+\sqrt{\eta}w)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the negative log-density of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> has Hessian
<math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+\nabla g_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+\nabla g_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log q_{y}(w)=-(w+g_{y}(w))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\alpha\eta I\preceq\nabla g_{y}(w)\preceq\beta\eta I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log q_{y}(w)=-(w+g_{y}(w))\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\alpha\eta I\preceq\nabla g_{y}(w)\preceq\beta\eta I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly log-concave. We use the same
symbol <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for the conditional half-turn operator in the
normalized coordinate <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=(x-y)/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=(x-y)/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{H}_{y}f)(w)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f\Bigl(\frac{x^{\prime}-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(y+\sqrt{\eta}w,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{H}_{y}f)(w)\coloneqq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f\Bigl(\frac{x^{\prime}-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}\Bigr)\,\mathcal{H}_{y}(y+\sqrt{\eta}w,\mathrm{d}x^{\prime})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 3.2 (Reversibility of the conditional half-turn kernel). ‣ 3.2 The ideal conditional half-turn process ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is a self-adjoint Markov
contraction on <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Put</p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}W\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}W\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional covariance in the normalized
coordinate; equivalently, we have the identity
<math id="A3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)=\eta\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)=\eta\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}=\eta\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}=\eta\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">by (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation D.10 ‣ Hessian of the augmented marginal. ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a>). Thus <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is both the covariance
defect relative to a standard Gaussian and the normalized curvature of
the <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>-marginal. For <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="A3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>; this affine function has mean zero
under <math id="A3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The main result of this subsection is the following estimate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Uniformly in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, every
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}:w\mapsto a^{\top}(w-\bar{w}_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">More generally, suppose that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is measurable and
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(x,y)\coloneqq a_{y}^{\top}\Bigl(\frac{x-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}-\bar{w}_{y}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(x,y)\coloneqq a_{y}^{\top}\Bigl(\frac{x-y}{\sqrt{\eta}}-\bar{w}_{y}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\ell\|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\ell\|^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\int a_{y}^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a_{y}\,\pi_{\eta}^{Y}(\mathrm{d}y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the proposition after two preparatory results. The first gives a
Duhamel representation of the deviation from exact sign reversal; the
second bounds the resulting term in terms of <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, first fix a reference point
<math id="A3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> in the rescaled coordinate. The resulting
phase-space process is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\dot{w}=p\,,\qquad\dot{p}=-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}\,,\\
\text{event rate }[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\,,\\
p\longmapsto R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p\quad\text{at a bounce}\,.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.300em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">˙</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.300em">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>event rate </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mtext>at a bounce</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.300em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\dot{w}=p\,,\qquad\dot{p}=-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}\,,\\
\text{event rate }[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\,,\\
p\longmapsto R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p\quad\text{at a bounce}\,.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">The construction and path reversal arguments of
Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Conditional half-turn process: construction, invariance, and implementation ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> apply verbatim, with phase space
law <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the resulting strongly continuous
contraction semigroup by
<math id="A3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>. On smooth compactly
supported observables, its generator is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}f(w,p)&amp;\coloneqq p^{\top}\nabla_{w}f(w,p)-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}^{\top}\nabla_{p}f(w,p)\\
&amp;\qquad{}+[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\bigl\{f(w,R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p)-f(w,p)\bigr\}\,.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>w</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.022em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}f(w,p)&amp;\coloneqq p^{\top}\nabla_{w}f(w,p)-\{w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}^{\top}\nabla_{p}f(w,p)\\
&amp;\qquad{}+[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}\bigl\{f(w,R_{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})}p)-f(w,p)\bigr\}\,.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The operator <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is
recovered by drawing <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, running the corresponding
process for time <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and averaging over <math id="A3.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math> and the
initial Gaussian momentum.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}=\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}=\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the bounce
rate vanishes. The dynamics reduce to harmonic motion,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}=w_{0}\cos t+p_{0}\sin t\,,\hskip 20.00003ptp_{t}=-w_{0}\sin t+p_{0}\cos t\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}=w_{0}\cos t+p_{0}\sin t\,,\hskip 20.00003ptp_{t}=-w_{0}\sin t+p_{0}\cos t\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}(w_{\pi})=-\ell_{a,y}(w_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}(w_{\pi})=-\ell_{a,y}(w_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. For general <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
discrepancy between the harmonic center <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math> and the
conditional mean <math id="A3.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with the residual gradient
bounces, produces an inhomogeneous term. The next lemma identifies this
term.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Affine Duhamel formula)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, set</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq-a^{\top}\{\bar{w}_{y}+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}-2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq-a^{\top}\{\bar{w}_{y}+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}-2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the quotient is defined as zero when
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}(w)=g_{y}(\widetilde{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}(w)=g_{y}(\widetilde{w})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>, and for every
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{w}})\ell_{a,y}=\int_{0}^{\pi}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin s\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{w}})\ell_{a,y}=\int_{0}^{\pi}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin s\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The generator maps the position observable <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math> to the
momentum observable <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}p</annotation></semantics></math>, and maps <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\top}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}p</annotation></semantics></math> back to
<math id="A3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, this pair evolves as a harmonic
system with the additional term <math id="A3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and variation of
constants gives the claimed formula. We first establish the required
<math id="A3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds and justify these generator identities for the unbounded
observables.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> is square integrable. Its first term is
constant in <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w,p)</annotation></semantics></math>, while the absolute value of its second term is at
most</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{|a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}|}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\,[p^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}]_{+}^{2}\,\frac{|a^{\top}\{g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\}|}{\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|g_{y}(w)-g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\beta\eta\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|w-\widetilde{w}\|\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\beta\eta\,\|a\|\,\|p\|^{2}\,\|w-\widetilde{w}\|\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly log-concave and the momentum is Gaussian,
this bound shows that <math id="A3.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to
<math id="A3.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>. The same moment bounds give
<math id="A3.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\in L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a^{\top}(R_{h}p-p)=-2(p^{\top}h)(a^{\top}h)/\|h\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\top}(R_{h}p-p)=-2(p^{\top}h)(a^{\top}h)/\|h\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[u]_{+}u=[u]_{+}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[u]_{+}u=[u]_{+}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the generator formula gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a^{\top}p\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)=-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a^{\top}p\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)=-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">To justify these identities for the unbounded observables, set <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\{\|w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}+\|p\|^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\widetilde{w}}(w,p)\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\{\|w+g_{y}(\widetilde{w})\|^{2}+\|p\|^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is preserved by both the flow and the bounces. Let <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be
a smooth cutoff equal to one on <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,R]</annotation></semantics></math> and zero on
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2R,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2R,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Conservation of <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives, for
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\in\{\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\in\{\ell_{a,y},a^{\top}p\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A3.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\{\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})F\}=\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})\,\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖫</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}\{\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})F\}=\chi_{R}(H_{\widetilde{w}})\,\mathsf{L}_{y,\widetilde{w}}F</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying Dynkin’s formula and then letting <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
using the preceding integrability bounds and semigroup contractivity,
yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}-\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}-\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)\,\mathrm{d}s\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)\,\mathrm{d}s\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)-a^{\top}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(a^{\top}p)-a^{\top}p</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}})\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}(-\ell_{a,y}+k_{a,\widetilde{w}})\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying variation of constants to this integral system gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}\ell_{a,y}=\ell_{a,y}\cos t+a^{\top}p\sin t+\int_{0}^{t}\mathsf{T}_{s}^{y,\widetilde{w}}k_{a,\widetilde{w}}\sin(t-s)\,\mathrm{d}s\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">This is the first identity in the lemma. At <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, the homogeneous
part is <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\ell_{a,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\ell_{a,y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sin(\pi-s)=\sin s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sin(\pi-s)=\sin s</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives
(<a href="#A3.E12" title="Equation C.12 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Affine Duhamel formula). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> will also use the
following identities and bounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional gradient covariance bound)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(g_{y}(W))\preceq\frac{\beta\eta}{1-\beta\eta}\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\preceq 2\beta\eta\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}_{q_{y}}(g_{y}(W))\preceq\frac{\beta\eta}{1-\beta\eta}\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\preceq 2\beta\eta\,(I-\Sigma_{y})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{+}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{+}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=y+\sqrt{\eta}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=y+\sqrt{\eta}W</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{-}=y+2\sqrt{\eta}W</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying (<a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation C.9 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>) to
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:u\mapsto F((u-y)/(2\sqrt{\eta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:u\mapsto F((u-y)/(2\sqrt{\eta}))</annotation></semantics></math> therefore gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}\nabla F(W)=\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}[F(W)\,\{W+g_{y}(W)\}]\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}\nabla F(W)=\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}[F(W)\,\{W+g_{y}(W)\}]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math> and then the coordinate functions of <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{y}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{y}(W)</annotation></semantics></math>, with the same cutoff approximation as in
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathbb{E}\nabla g_{y}(W)=I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathrm{Cov}(W,g_{y}(W))=I-\Sigma_{y}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\mathbb{E}\nabla g_{y}(W)=I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="A3.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the same conditional Poincaré estimate used in
the proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, together with
<math id="A3.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\nabla g_{y})^{2}\preceq\beta\eta\,\nabla g_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.317em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla g_{y})^{2}\preceq\beta\eta\,\nabla g_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> then give</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))a</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\|\nabla g_{y}(W)\,a\|^{2}\leq\beta\eta\,a^{\top}\{I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\}a\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\|\nabla g_{y}(W)\,a\|^{2}\leq\beta\eta\,a^{\top}\{I-\Sigma_{y}+\mathrm{Cov}(g_{y}(W))\}a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging proves (<a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation C.13 ‣ Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.13</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A3.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}\sim q_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent of
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,P)\sim q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,P)\sim q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. We first apply the Duhamel formula to
identify the estimate that remains to be proved. Using, in order,
Jensen’s inequality in <math id="A3.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A3.E12" title="Equation C.12 ‣ Lemma C.3 (Affine Duhamel formula). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.12</span></a>), the Bochner triangle inequality,
the contractivity of Gaussian momentum averaging and
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A3.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\pi}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\pi}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(I+\mathsf{H}_{y})\ell_{a,y}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\bigl\|\mathbb{E}_{P}[(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{W}})\ell_{a,y}]\bigr\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\bigl\|\mathbb{E}_{P}[(I+\mathsf{T}_{\pi}^{y,\widetilde{W}})\ell_{a,y}]\bigr\|_{L^{2}(q_{y})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\Bigl(\int_{0}^{\pi}\|\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{W}}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr)^{2}\leq 4\,\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\widetilde{W}}\Bigl(\int_{0}^{\pi}\|\mathsf{T}_{t}^{y,\widetilde{W}}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\|_{L^{2}(q_{y}\otimes\mathcal{N}(0,I))}\sin t\,\mathrm{d}t\Bigr)^{2}\leq 4\,\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to bound the second moment on the right.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conditional on <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,\widetilde{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,\widetilde{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, a direct calculation with the
Gaussian momentum <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, together with
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)=-\bar{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> from
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{P}[k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{P}[k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)\}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.150em">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{y}}g_{y}(W)\}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Var_{P}(k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Var_{P}(k_{a,\widetilde{W}}\mid W,\widetilde{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=5\,[a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-g_{y}(\widetilde{W})\}]^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=5\,[a^{\top}\{g_{y}(W)-g_{y}(\widetilde{W})\}]^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">After averaging over the independent variables <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional variance term contributes
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))</annotation></semantics></math>, while the squared conditional mean
contributes one more copy of the same variance. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}=11\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}=11\Var_{q_{y}}(a^{\top}g_{y}(W))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4 (Conditional gradient covariance bound). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo mathsize="1.280em">~</mo></mover></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{W,\widetilde{W},P}k_{a,\widetilde{W}}^{2}\leq C\beta\eta\,a^{\top}(I-\Sigma_{y})a\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the last estimate with the Duhamel bound proves
(<a href="#A3.E11" title="Equation C.11 ‣ Proposition C.2 (Weighted half-turn estimate for affine functions). ‣ C.2 The half-turn operator on affine functions ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.11</span></a>). For the global
assertion, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law). ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> gives
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I-\Sigma_{y}\succeq\alpha\eta\,(1+\alpha\eta)^{-1}\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I-\Sigma_{y}\succeq\alpha\eta\,(1+\alpha\eta)^{-1}\,I</annotation></semantics></math>, so the stated
integrability condition implies <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in L^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Its
conditional mean is zero. Applying the conditional inequality with
<math id="A3.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and integrating in <math id="A3.SS2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> proves the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>